<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco Maria I della Rovere</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1490–1538</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco Maria I della Rovere was a nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-julius-ii">Pope Julius II</a>, who arranged his adoption by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guidobaldo-da-montefeltro">Guidobaldo da Montefeltro</a>. He inherited the Duchy of Urbino in 1508 and received Pesaro in 1512. Pope Leo X drove him out in 1516, but he recovered the duchy in 1521, made Pesaro his main residence and commanded the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francesco-maria-i-della-rovere.jpg" alt="Francesco Maria I della Rovere" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Titian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Francesco_Maria_della_Rovere,_Duke_of_Urbino_(by_Titian)_%E2%80%93_Galleria_degli_Uffizi,_Florence.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
